# Trivy vulnerability ignore list. Every entry must justify itself — this file
# is reviewed as part of the security scan output, not a place to silence
# noise.

# CVE-2024-23342 (ecdsa / python-ecdsa): Minerva timing side-channel in ECDSA
# signing/verification. `ecdsa` is a *mandatory* transitive dependency of
# python-jose (backend/app/core/security.py) regardless of which install extra
# is used, and upstream has stated they won't fix side-channel issues in the
# pure-Python implementation (see the advisory). We never exercise the
# vulnerable code path: every jwt.decode() call in this codebase hardcodes
# `algorithms=["RS256"]` (RSA, not ECDSA) — see app/core/security.py. Revisit
# if the codebase ever adds an ECDSA-based algorithm, or when migrating off
# python-jose.
CVE-2024-23342
